# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# The working tree here is Windows and the sources are LF, so without this every
# file Git touches warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF" — 130 of them on the
# first add — and the first commit from a Linux machine would then show all 178
# files as modified with no content change.
#
# `text=auto` stores LF in the object database and checks out the platform's
# native ending, which is the one setting that makes the diff mean something on
# both sides.
* text=auto

# Generated. Collapsed in diffs and excluded from the language stats, so a
# 6,000-line lockfile churn does not bury an actual change in a review.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated=true
backend/package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated=true
